  "slug": "spin-altermagnetism-d7e3",
  "summary": "Eight preprints propose symmetry-sensitive probes and magnon-based functionalities in altermagnets, spin-nematics, noncoplanar and multiferroic magnets.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is theoretical identification of measurable responses that expose or exploit unconventional magnetic order. For altermagnets and noncoplanar antiferromagnets, octupolar magneto-optical effects are proposed as field-free probes, and nonlinear spin generation and spin photocurrent as probes of spin-space symmetry, domains and quantum geometry. Twist engineering of collinear bilayers is proposed to yield quasicrystalline altermagnets with high-order spin polarization. On the magnon side, single magnons and bound magnon pairs in pyrochlore spin-nematics give competing Berry-curvature thermal Hall contributions with field-tunable sign reversal; CrI3 nanotubes in an axial field acquire a conical phase and a large pseudo-orbital magnon moment; and gated domain boundaries in BiFeO3 modulate nonreciprocal magnons in a proposed transistor. Cavity photon condensation from scalar spin chirality and defect-enhanced orbital magnetoelectric responses are more peripheral. All items are preprints.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-21"
}
